@ptomato Since you quoted from  [#5488](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/5488#issuecomment-1425523050) and gave authoritative advice I guess I had presumed you were a WHATWG member. 

I see you're 'Temporal' and speaking from experience with that, while tracking this issue.   

Thanks for the tip on how to proceed, maybe from your inspiration @annevk and @hsivonen can see that the criteria have largely been met.

@Wigny  You are hand coding but are  you using AI like with [Ona](https://ona.com/) ? 

Useful agents came about after this input-duration effort was started ... it would be amazing to have a mashup of the repos listed here.  Several have useful features and HTML still doesn't have an input duration type.  

It might not take that much effort.  I would be happy to take pull requests and rebase or maybe delegate the input-duration npm to your repo.
